#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5ee3c3f-4289-5e38-a47a-52e5c2ad3817" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding the Odd Extension of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f7af1dba-6300-56ab-93d2-0f3d1b893dad" :question/math-academy-id "e-21809" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=x^2+10x$ for $[MATH: x\\in[0,6),]$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x \\in (-6,6)$. What is the value of $f(-1)$?" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $[MATH: x\\in[0,6),]$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n$[MATH: {F(x), \\mid x ∈ [0, 6),; - F(-x), \\mid x ∈ (-6, 0).]$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in(-6,0)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= -F(-x) \\\\\n&= - ((-x)^{2} + 10(-x)) \\\\\n&= - (x^{2} - 10x) \\\\\n&=-x^{2} + 10x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-1) &= - (-1)^{2} + 10(-1) =-11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166500 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a85c9c4-8563-55e0-9d4f-7d61d3be6243" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Sine Coefficients From the Half-Range Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "1ff70a32-336a-5ff2-bfe8-0df06eec1a7c" :question/math-academy-id "e-21810" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=4x$ for $[MATH: x\\in[0,\\pi).]$ Find the missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$AAAAA_{A}^{A}$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\nb_n=\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi f(x)\\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nf(x)=4x\n$$\n\nfor $x \\in (0,\\pi)$. So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nb_n = \\dfrac{8}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi x \\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & ⇒u^{′} = 1 \\\\ v^{′} = \\sin (nx) & ⇒v =-\\frac{1}{n}\\cos (nx)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb_{n} &= \\left.\\frac{8}{π}(uv\\right|_{0}^{π} - \\int_{0}^{π}vu^{′}dx) \\\\\n&= \\frac{8}{π}(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\cos (nx)]_{0}^{π} + \\frac{1}{n}\\int_{0}^{π}\\cos (nx)dx) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{8}{nπ}((π \\cdot \\cos (nπ) - 0 \\cdot \\cos (0)) - \\frac{1}{n}[\\sin (nx)]_{0}^{π}) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{8}{nπ}(π\\cos (nπ) - \\frac{1}{n}(\\sin (nπ) - \\sin (0))) \\\\\n&= - (8\\cos (nπ))/(n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n\\cos(n\\pi)=(-1)^n\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\nb_n = -\\dfrac{8(-1)^n}{n}=\\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n}\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n} \\cdot \\sin(nx)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a85c9c4-8563-55e0-9d4f-7d61d3be6243" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Sine Coefficients From the Half-Range Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8590e119-0a06-5d5b-8b1e-5a6edacfc4ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos (πx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164888} {:answer/id #uuid "f98c1985-dd30-5c3b-a5c7-b30d18fb8035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin (nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164889} {:answer/id #uuid "5517755f-5376-584c-bfd5-e36f4d34876d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin (πx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164890} {:answer/id #uuid "63f41640-412f-57df-8aaa-92588874897e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos (nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f98c1985-dd30-5c3b-a5c7-b30d18fb8035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin (nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164889} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4265b0-d9b8-565c-a28d-2142be502e9c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4f00093-5bf5-53bf-b020-6c033978ec9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(1 − (− 1)^{n}))/(πn)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164893} {:answer/id #uuid "d511eb65-fcb2-5653-8aee-87de44c4ed02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10(− 1)^{n})/(n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164894} {:answer/id #uuid "0744d591-06a8-5134-93c2-364d44611dd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10(1 − (− 1)^{n}))/(πn)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164895} {:answer/id #uuid "0a7fd1e6-79f7-5313-a944-32349963d83b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(− 1)^{n})/(n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d511eb65-fcb2-5653-8aee-87de44c4ed02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10(− 1)^{n})/(n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164894} :answer-field/id #uuid "68012043-0dd6-5b01-bdec-4d15aac25762" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164892}] :question/id #uuid "37a89f3d-e2cd-5d21-bb53-6d99da952356" :question/math-academy-id "q-340629" :question/problem "Let $F(x) =-5x$ for $[MATH: x ∈ [0, π).]$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2π$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.$(2(-1)^{n})/(n)$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}"}]}
